From bb778942690e0c6a6f17c03c21212378073e5d59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 15:02:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Added: Add termux.properties settings for the terminal tabs
 and moving tabs

- terminal-tabs = top | bottom | off: where to show the tab bar, or hide it
- terminal-tabs-show-close = true | false: whether tabs have a close button
- max-sessions = 1..32: the maximum number of sessions, 8 by default like before

The settings are read from the properties file by the fork-only
TerminalTabsSettings and reloaded by termux-reload-settings. Toasts for
switching sessions and title changes are shown again when the tab bar is
off. A tab's long press menu can also move it left or right, which
changes the order of the sessions in the drawer too.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GLNsTPnn2xKUQ4uFcevT6G
---
 app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/TermuxActivity.java         | 5 ++++-
 .../com/termux/app/terminal/TermuxTerminalSessionClient.java | 5 ++---
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/TermuxActivity.java b/app/src/main/java/com/termux/app/TermuxActivity.java
